# Package Structure

```
laragentic/
├── src/
│   ├── Loops/
│   │   ├── ReActLoop.php              # ReAct loop trait (core)
│   │   ├── LoopResult.php             # Wraps AgentResponse with loop metadata
│   │   └── LoopStep.php               # Single iteration value object
│   ├── Concerns/
│   │   └── HasCallbacks.php           # Lifecycle callback registration trait
│   ├── Contracts/
│   │   └── Loop.php                   # Loop contract/interface
│   ├── Exceptions/
│   │   └── MaxIterationsExceededException.php
│   └── LaragenticServiceProvider.php
├── config/
│   └── agentic.php                    # Package configuration
├── tests/
│   ├── Unit/Loops/
│   ├── Feature/
│   ├── Pest.php
│   └── TestCase.php
├── .cursor/rules/                     # AI assistant rules
├── composer.json
├── phpunit.xml
├── LICENSE
└── README.md
```

## Conventions

- **Loop traits** that agents `use` go in `src/Loops/` (e.g. `ReActLoop`)
- **Supporting traits** (e.g. `HasCallbacks`) go in `src/Concerns/`
- **Value objects** for loop data (`LoopResult`, `LoopStep`) live alongside their loop in `src/Loops/`
- **Contracts/interfaces** go in `src/Contracts/`
- **Exceptions** go in `src/Exceptions/`
- Mirror the Laravel AI SDK naming style: traits are verbs/nouns (`RemembersConversations`), contracts are interfaces
- The service provider registers config and any bindings
- Tests mirror the `src/` structure under `tests/`
